 ## Browser organization and invariants
 
+### Positional Servo (MS62)
+The only supported servo is the positional MS62 on X1 DO2 / Arduino D4.
+On holds the verified 1056 µs target. Off commands 1944 µs for about one second,
+then suppresses PWM (targets nominally 120° apart). The firmware timer counts
+SERVO_OFF_SETTLE_FRAMES = 50; this is a settling allowance, not arrival feedback.
+Stopping PWM may not remove this digital servo's holding torque; verify physically.
+Edit SERVO_ON_US and SERVO_OFF_US in controllino_motion_control.ino to calibrate.
+Startup sends no pulses; Stop signal, M and E-STOP suppress PWM, not power.
+There is no external angle feedback. Closing the browser leaves On held;
+Off still finishes its settling interval and stops PWM without the browser.
+The browser has no servo heartbeat, motion timer, or continuous-rotation mode.
+The /api/stepper/servo/position endpoint accepts an explicit boolean on.
+V1 T1400/T1600 wire tokens are retained for deployed-controller compatibility;
+they select targets, not literal pulse widths. Old J/P/B1 commands are rejected.
+The original Yún dashboard and its shared ESC transport remain separate.
+The positional-only firmware was compiled, regression-tested and flashed on
+2026-09-15 after the requested dashboard shutdown. Upload verification passed;
+startup telemetry confirmed servo PWM off, stepper disabled and R5 off.
+Off-settling update flashed 2026-09-15; upload verification and 123 tests passed.
+Uploaded SHA-256: `dcb4c05a60c12fc852cb42a1d10691e555a390dc51cc99adcf8c2c59e9455773`.
+
+### Shared behavior
+
+- On Controllino installations, **Solenoid 4** (button/key 4) controls **R5 /
+  Arduino 27** through `V1 K0/K1`. Other solenoids remain on ESP32. Relay 5
+  starts Off and E-STOP de-energizes it. Status `r5` reports the commanded coil
+  state, not contact feedback. The merged legacy field `esp32_sol4` now carries
+  that relay state so existing UI, recordings and SICK open-flow calculations
+  keep working; there is no fallback to ESP32 channel 4 if Controllino is absent.
+
 - `createActions` owns keyed pending state, duplicate suppression, errors and
